{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ומחה", :translit "u'macha", :gloss "and he shall blot out"} {:he "ומחה אל מי המרים", :translit "u'macha el mei ha-marim", :gloss "and he shall blot out against the bitter water"} {:he "ומחה על כתף ים כנרת", :translit "u'macha al katef yam kineret", :gloss "and he shall blot out upon the shoulder of the Sea of Kinneret"} {:he "ומחה ה' אלהים דמעה מעל כל פנים", :translit "u'macha Hashem Elohim dim'ah me'al kol panim", :gloss "and Hashem Elohim shall blot out a tear from upon every face"} {:he "ומחה ה' את שמו", :translit "u'macha Hashem et shemo", :gloss "and Hashem shall blot out His name"} {:he "מים חיים", :translit "mayim chayim", :gloss "living waters"} {:he "מקדם לעין", :translit "mikedem la'ayin", :gloss "from before the spring"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Four-fold gezeirah shavah on the word ומחה linking Sotah water, Kinneret spring, tear, and divine name erasure"}], :frame {:text "The phrase ומחה occurs four times in Scripture, and Ba'al HaTurim reads each occurrence as revealing a different outcome for the Sotah. If she is guilty, her fate parallels the erasure of God's name in the water — as the Torah commands the priest to write curses including the divine name on a scroll and dissolve them in the bitter water (Numbers 5:23). If she is innocent, God wipes away every tear, as stated 'ומחה ה' אלהים דמעה מעל כל פנים' (Isaiah 25:8). If she was barren she now conceives, and if she previously gave birth with difficulty she now gives birth easily. These outcomes for the innocent Sotah are taught in the Mishnah: if she was barren she is remembered, if she had difficult births she now gives birth easily (Sotah 3:4 in the Bavli at Sotah 26a). The link between the Sotah's bitter water and living waters is also addressed at Sotah 16b–17a, where the requirement of 'mayim chayim' (Numbers 5:18) is debated. The Sea of Kinneret passage is at Deuteronomy 3:17, with 'mikedem la'ayin' at Deuteronomy 3:17.", :sources ["Numbers 5:18" "Numbers 5:23" "Deuteronomy 3:17" "Isaiah 25:8" "Mishnah Sotah 3:4" "Sotah 16b" "Sotah 26a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Four-fold gezeirah shavah on the word ומחה linking Sotah water, Kinneret spring, tear, and divine name erasure", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:27:07.778143550Z", :model "glm-5.2"}